## Scope

Close the unrestricted-public-registration blocker in #71 without changing frozen flight, Heart Point, matchmaking, rating-calculation, or release-governance semantics.

## Account lifecycle

- publish factual `PRIVACY.md` data-handling notice;
- expose the same account-data notice before registration and from authenticated Account & Privacy UI;
- add authenticated self-service deletion requiring current password + exact `DELETE`;
- revoke all account sessions on deletion;
- anonymize login/display identity, credential material, and aircraft preferences;
- retain only pseudonymous internal user ID + rated-match/rating ledger needed for referential and ranking integrity;
- exclude deleted accounts from login, authenticated sessions, and leaderboard;
- opportunistically clean expired session rows during account activity;
- add `0003_account_lifecycle.sql` with deletion-state schema/indexes.

## School / QA parity

- mirror deletion/anonymization behavior in school-local account store/backend;
- extend C4D school account smoke to verify password confirmation, session revocation, login rejection, and leaderboard exclusion;
- add `pnpm verify:public:account` and run it in Project CI;
- extend C5E Auth/Home observations to cover privacy notice and account deletion UI.

## Privacy boundary

The notice documents only fields actually present in the application account contract. No email, legal-name, address, phone, age, or location fields are added.

## Production boundary

This PR performs no D1 provisioning, remote migration, deploy, rollback, secret/environment mutation, or other production action. The migration remains source-only until the governed C4D provisioning gate is explicitly authorized.

