## Objective

Supersede the parallel step-093 drafts with one stricter candidate: retain the filesystem durability and delivery hardening proven by #678, while adding a crash-safe firing/resolved incident lifecycle that does not lose alerts, duplicate incident generations after a crash, or suppress same-window recurrence after recovery.

## Parent / fail-closed posture

Built from Draft PR #678 exact head `74b821c923e50742cefa16c335dbdb88061286bc`, where 11/12 protected workflows are green and only `AI Tenant RLS Runtime Evidence` remains waiting on the protected environment gate.

The underlying #677 parent likewise remains conditional on its protected RLS evidence.

This PR is Draft and temporarily targets `main` only to obtain complete cumulative exact-head evidence. No merge or deployment is authorized.

## Incident identity v2

Step 093 remains `0109_operational_signal_envelope.sql`, but because it is not deployed, its contract is tightened before promotion:

- `incident_key`: stable identity of the monitored condition, independent of changing reason codes;
- `condition_fingerprint`: normalized critical severity + reason-set fingerprint;
- `incident_id`: unique 64-hex incident generation;
- `signal_id`: deterministic from incident generation + firing/resolved lifecycle;
- unique `incident_id + lifecycle` database authority;
- exact payload-hash conflict rejection in PostgreSQL as well as the filesystem spool.

A changed critical cause rotates the incident generation. A recovered condition closes the active generation. The same condition recurring after recovery creates a new generation even inside the same former dedupe window.

## Crash-safe transition protocol

The condition-state file uses a write-ahead transition intent:

1. validate desired transition and construct the exact immutable signal;
2. atomically write + fsync a private pending transition containing the exact payload;
3. enqueue that exact signal into the durable local spool;
4. atomically commit the next active state;
5. remove idle state after a resolved transition.

If the process crashes before or after enqueue, the next invocation replays the exact pending signal/incident ID. It cannot commit active state for a signal that was never durably enqueued, and it does not create a random duplicate generation after a crash.

## Mentor detector authority

The independent health probe is the sole durable incident producer and governs three independent conditions:

- `mentor_profile_projection`;
- `mentor_profile_database_authority`;
- `mentor_profile_health_probe`.

Warning from idle does not page. Warning/healthy resolves an existing critical projection incident. Database recovery resolves the database-authority incident. Unexpected probe failure has its own incident identity.

The worker remains telemetry-only and does not compete with the durable rail.

## Retained #678 transport guarantees

- filesystem-first outage-safe delivery;
- fsync + atomic publication/archive movement;
- 0600 files / 0700 directories and ancestor-symlink defense;
- due-before-limit fairness;
- persisted local delivery-attempt history;
- crash recovery after delivered/terminal attempts without webhook redelivery;
- deterministic capped retry jitter;
- HTTPS, stable Idempotency-Key, bounded timeout/attempts;
- quarantine for poison/terminal/exhausted items;
- PostgreSQL remains a best-effort immutable forensic mirror;
- production bundles and DB-independent delivery preflight;
- governed EnvironmentFile parsing and fail-closed systemd installers.

## New permanent evidence

- firing dedupe;
- critical cause rotation;
- resolution;
- same-hour recurrence after resolution creates a new incident;
- simulated enqueue crash followed by exact payload/incident replay;
- warning/healthy from idle never opens a durable incident;
- condition state excludes learner/tenant/workspace/conversation/KYC data;
- firing fingerprint override rejected;
- same-ID/different-payload PostgreSQL conflict rejected.

## Scope

This candidate supersedes the architectural direction of #679/#680; those drafts should not be merged independently if this v2 exact-head evidence passes.

Keep fail-closed.

No merge, staging deploy, production deploy, SLA/paging-policy activation, financial/custody activation or launch authorization is granted by this Draft.

