### E2E isolation
Chromium's native context-menu UI is not reliably automatable. The test build exposes a compile-time-only message hook that calls the exact same `captureFromContextMenu` handler registered with `chrome.contextMenus.onClicked`.

The E2E build also receives a localhost fixture host permission so automated injection does not rely on a toolbar-generated `activeTab` grant. Both the hook and that fixture permission are absent from the production build; `scripts/check-built.mjs` asserts that boundary on every normal `npm run check`.

### CI
The existing check job still runs typecheck, unit tests, production build, and production permission assertions. A second job installs Chromium, builds the isolated E2E variant, and runs the extension suite under Xvfb.

