## Summary

This workflow-governance tranche addresses stale Gaze-in-the-Wild PR queues without weakening any scientific/source gate.

### Trigger scope

Removes only generic `mkdocs.yml` changes from these focused workflows:

- `gaze-in-wild-first-party-readiness.yml`
- `gaze-in-wild-exact-copy-review.yml`
- `gaze-in-wild-figshare-distribution-rights.yml`

Strict Docs continues to validate MkDocs/site navigation. All GIW-specific source, evidence, validation, test, probe, documentation, and workflow-file triggers remain present.

### Concurrency

Adds the same PR/ref-scoped concurrency model already used by CI/Docs:

```yaml
concurrency:
  group: ${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.event.pull_request.number || github.ref }}
  cancel-in-progress: true
```

This means:
- a newer commit on the same PR supersedes obsolete queued/running generations;
- distinct PR numbers remain isolated;
- branch/ref generations remain isolated;
- one focused workflow cannot cancel another because `github.workflow` is part of the group.

### Regression contract

Adds `tests/test_giw_workflow_governance.py` to protect:

- no generic `mkdocs.yml` fan-out;
- PR/ref-scoped concurrency;
- `cancel-in-progress: true`;
- retained `workflow_dispatch`;
- retained material GIW source/test/evidence/workflow paths;
- retained fail-closed focused test/evidence commands.

## Scientific/quality boundary

No source availability, rights, exact-copy, quarantine, publication, empirical-evidence, or scientific-review gate is removed or weakened. The change affects workflow scheduling/trigger scope only.

## Local validation completed

A local minimal repository containing the exact three proposed workflow files and the governance regression was validated before repository writes:

- YAML parsing: pass for all three workflows;
- `pytest -q tests/test_giw_workflow_governance.py`: **3 passed**;
- concurrency group identity: verified;
- `cancel-in-progress: true`: verified;
- `workflow_dispatch`: verified;
- material trigger paths: verified;
- focused fail-closed commands: verified.

A full local clone/full-suite run is not available in this execution environment because the container cannot resolve `github.com`; that infrastructure limitation is not treated as a code result.

## GitHub CI certification

